WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.274
Hold a conversation.

00:00:01.274 --> 00:00:05.161
Notice how quickly you respond to what the other person says.

00:00:05.161 --> 00:00:10.386
The gap between their last word and your first is usually less than half a second.

00:00:10.386 --> 00:00:15.037
When it stretches past two seconds, you both feel it — the air goes flat.

00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:17.776
Beyond ten seconds, you've stopped talking.

00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:20.134
You're taking turns leaving messages.

00:00:20.134 --> 00:00:25.486
The radio signal between Earth and the Moon takes one point three seconds , one way.

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:27.652
Two point six seconds, round trip.

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:34.406
Walter Cronkite's broadcasts during Apollo 11 had a noticeable pause every time Houston spoke to the crew.

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:36.063
The astronauts spoke back.

00:00:36.063 --> 00:00:37.018
The pause held.

00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:39.121
The conversation worked — barely.

00:00:39.121 --> 00:00:41.924
Now imagine you tried to drive a Mars rover.

00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:46.512
One-way light time to Mars at average distance: about fourteen minutes .

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:49.060
Round trip: about twenty-eight minutes .

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.972
You push the joystick forward.

00:00:50.972 --> 00:00:53.329
Nothing happens for fourteen minutes.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:55.177
Then the rover starts moving.

00:00:55.177 --> 00:00:58.108
You see it moving fourteen minutes after that.

00:00:58.108 --> 00:01:05.754
By the time your "stop" command arrives, the rover has been driving — by your now-stale instructions — for half an hour.

00:01:05.754 --> 00:01:08.876
This is why there is no manual mode on the rover.

00:01:08.876 --> 00:01:09.832
There can't be.

00:01:09.832 --> 00:01:16.267
The rover has to think for itself in every short interval between the planning team's daily commands.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:23.913
Beyond a couple of light-seconds of distance, every spacecraft humanity has ever sent has had to become its own captain.

00:01:23.913 --> 00:01:25.059
The Moon is close.

00:01:25.059 --> 00:01:25.824
Mars is not.

